WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.987
Stop conditions are part of the algorithm, not an afterthought.

00:00:03.987 --> 00:00:10.862
A successful stop might be evidence is sufficient, the answer has been generated, and validation passed.

00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:15.587
A safe failure stop might be no approved evidence exists.

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:18.953
A budget stop might be maximum steps reached.

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:25.651
If a tool fails temporarily, the policy may allow one or two bounded retries.

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:32.376
If a high-impact action is requested, the workflow may stop and wait for human approval.

00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:37.561
For example, an assistant can explain that a refund appears appropriate,

00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:43.181
but issuing the refund may require an authorized human or a separate approval rule.

00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:49.153
If you cannot describe how your workflow stops, the workflow is not finished.

00:00:49.153 --> 00:00:51.827
Every loop needs a reachable exit.
